From: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] pci: qcom: optimize IPQ9574 PCIe Gen3 equalization and link training

================================================================================
MAXNET High-Performance Kernel Engine & Hardware Architecture Optimization
Engineered & Developed by Mahendra Mali (Max) for MAXNET Router OS
Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
================================================================================

On Qualcomm IPQ9574 / IPQ9554 enterprise networking platforms, the Qualcomm
PCIe 2.9.0 controller interfaces with high-speed Wi-Fi 6/6E radio companion
endpoints (such as QCN9074).

During Gen3 (8.0 GT/s) link negotiation in Linux 6.18, the standard controller
driver clears GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL during common equalization,
causing non-compliant endpoint receiver detection to fail with LTSSM stalling
in DETECT_QUIET state.

This MAXNET custom patch:
1. Retains GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL during equalization setup to
   guarantee immediate Gen3 link synchronization.
2. Provides a post-PERST deassertion settling interval allowing auxiliary
   clocks, receiver terminations, and endpoint power rails to stabilize.

Signed-off-by: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom-common.c | 4 +++-
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c        | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom-common.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom-common.c
@@ -31,7 +31,9 @@ void qcom_pcie_common_set_equalization(s
 		}
 
 		reg = dw_pcie_readl_dbi(pci, GEN3_RELATED_OFF);
-		reg &= ~GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL;
+		/* MAXNET Optimization by Mahendra Mali (Max): enforce Gen3 ZRXDC for QCN9074 */
+		reg |= GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL;
 		reg &= ~GEN3_RELATED_OFF_RATE_SHADOW_SEL_MASK;
 		reg |= FIELD_PREP(GEN3_RELATED_OFF_RATE_SHADOW_SEL_MASK,
 			  speed - PCIE_SPEED_8_0GT);
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -305,6 +305,10 @@ static void qcom_ep_reset_deassert(struc
 	/* Ensure that PERST has been asserted for at least 100 ms */
 	msleep(PCIE_T_PVPERL_MS);
 	qcom_perst_assert(pcie, false);
+	/* MAXNET Hardware Stabilization by Mahendra Mali (Max):
+	 * Allow endpoint clock, power rails and receiver detect to settle
+	 */
+	msleep(PCIE_T_PVPERL_MS);
 }
 
 static int qcom_pcie_start_link(struct dw_pcie *pci)
